<%/* Cookie notice.

     WHY THIS EXISTS: the site loads Microsoft Clarity on every page, and
     the Meta pixel whenever one is configured, and told nobody. Both are
     non-essential analytics and advertising technologies, and setting them
     without notice or a way to decline is a straightforward ePrivacy and
     GDPR problem for any EU or UK visitor, a CPRA problem in California,
     and a transparency problem for a Merchant Center reviewer regardless
     of jurisdiction.

     WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES: declining is real, not cosmetic. The choice is
     stored in localStorage and read by public/js/gogetcards.js before either
     tracker loads, so a visitor who declines is not measured. A banner
     that sets the cookies anyway is worse than no banner, because it turns
     an omission into a false statement.

     Accept and Decline are the same size, in the same style, side by side.
     Making refusal harder than acceptance is the pattern regulators
     specifically name, and it is not worth the handful of extra sessions.

     Rendered server-side but hidden by default; the script reveals it only
     when no choice has been recorded, so a returning visitor never sees it
     again and there is no flash of a banner for someone who already
     answered. */%>
<div class="cookie-notice" id="cookie-notice" role="region" aria-label="Cookie choices" hidden>
  <div class="cookie-notice__inner">
    <div class="cookie-notice__text">
      <p class="cookie-notice__title">We use a couple of non-essential cookies</p>
      <p class="cookie-notice__body">
        Essential cookies keep your cart working and cannot be turned off. Beyond that we
        use analytics to see where the site confuses people, and an advertising pixel when
        ads are running. Decline and neither one loads.
        <a href="<%= marketPath('/cookie-policy') %>">What each one does</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cookie-notice__actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="cookie-decline">Decline</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="cookie-accept">Accept</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<%/* Shown here, as the parser reaches it, rather than by the script bundle
     at the end of the body: the banner is the largest text on a phone's
     first screen, so waiting for the bundle delayed LCP by 250-700ms. */%>
<script>try{if(!localStorage.getItem('zy_cookie_consent'))document.getElementById('cookie-notice').hidden=false}catch(e){document.getElementById('cookie-notice').hidden=false}</script>

<style>
  .cookie-notice { position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 9000; background: var(--color-bg-elevated); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); box-shadow: 0 -8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); }
  .cookie-notice__inner { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2rem; }
  .cookie-notice__title { font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-heading); }
  .cookie-notice__body { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: 0.2rem; max-width: 68ch; }
  .cookie-notice__body a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  /* Equal weight, equal size. Declining must not be the harder path. */
  .cookie-notice__actions { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .cookie-notice__actions .btn { min-width: 6.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .cookie-notice__inner { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 0.9rem; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; }
    .cookie-notice__actions .btn { flex: 1; }
  }
</style>
